Managing Cisco infrastructure with Ansible requires understanding that different Cisco platforms (IOS, Nexus, ASA, etc.) use different Collections, Connection Methods, and Python Libraries.
Here is a structured breakdown of the modules, connectivity, and requirements for each platform you listed.
________________________________________
1. High-Level Connectivity Overview
Unlike managing Linux servers (which uses SSH+Python on the target), network devices are agentless and often don't have a Python interpreter you can use.
•	network_cli: Ansible logs into the device via SSH and "types" commands like a human operator. (Best for IOS, ASA, Nexus).
•	httpapi: Ansible sends structured JSON/XML data to the device's REST API. (Best for Nexus, Firepower, ISE).
________________________________________
2. Platform-Specific Breakdown
A. Cisco Routers & Switches (IOS / IOS-XE)
This is the most common category (Catalyst switches, ISR/ASR routers).
•	Collection Name: cisco.ios
•	Connection Method: network_cli (SSH)
•	Key Modules:
o	cisco.ios.ios_command: Run show commands (e.g., show ip int br).
o	cisco.ios.ios_config: Push configuration changes (global config mode).
o	cisco.ios.ios_l2_interfaces: Configure Layer 2 ports (Access/Trunk).
•	Requirement: SSH must be enabled on the device.
B. Cisco Nexus Switches (NX-OS)
Data center switches (Nexus 9k, 7k, 5k).
•	Collection Name: cisco.nxos
•	Connection Method:
o	httpapi (Recommended): Uses NX-API for faster, structured data return. Requires enabling feature nxapi on the switch.
o	network_cli: Standard SSH CLI interaction.
•	Key Modules:
o	cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans: Manage VLANs.
o	cisco.nxos.nxos_vrf: Manage VRFs.
o	cisco.nxos.nxos_vxlan_vtep: VXLAN configuration.
C. Cisco ASA Firewall
Legacy firewall management.
•	Collection Name: cisco.asa
•	Connection Method: network_cli (SSH) or httpapi (if REST API is enabled on ASA).
•	Key Modules:
o	cisco.asa.asa_acl: Manage Access Control Lists.
o	cisco.asa.asa_og: Manage Object Groups.
o	cisco.asa.asa_config: Push generic CLI configs.
•	Note: ASA automation is often limited compared to IOS; complex policies are easier to manage via asa_config blocks.
D. Cisco Firepower (FTD & FMC)
There are two ways to automate Firepower. Most enterprises use FMC (Firepower Management Center) to manage the FTD devices.
•	Collection Name: cisco.fmcansible (for FMC)
•	Connection Method: httpapi (REST API). Ansible talks to the FMC console, not the firewall directly.
•	Key Modules:
o	cisco.fmcansible.fmc_configuration: The "Swiss Army Knife" module used for almost all CRUD operations (Create/Read/Update/Delete) on objects, policies, and devices.
•	Requirement: You must enable REST API in FMC settings.
E. Cisco ISE (Identity Services Engine)
•	Collection Name: cisco.ise
•	Connection Method: local (The module runs locally on your machine and sends API calls to ISE).
•	Key Modules:
o	cisco.ise.network_device: Add/Remove Network Access Devices (NADs).
o	cisco.ise.endpoint_group: Manage endpoint identity groups.
•	Requirement: Requires the Python library ciscoisesdk.
________________________________________
3. Summary Configuration Table
Platform	Ansible Collection	Connection Type	Port	Python Dependencies
IOS / IOS-XE	cisco.ios	network_cli	22	paramiko or libssh
Nexus (NX-OS)	cisco.nxos	httpapi (or network_cli)	80/443	requests
ASA	cisco.asa	network_cli	22	paramiko
Firepower (FMC)	cisco.fmcansible	httpapi	443	requests
ISE	cisco.ise	local*	443	ciscoisesdk
*ISE modules technically run on the control node (localhost) and make API calls out to ISE, so ansible_connection is usually set to local.
________________________________________
4. Example Inventory & Playbook
To make this work, you need to define your inventory variables correctly.
inventory.ini
Ini, TOML
[ios_switches]
switch01 ansible_host=192.168.1.10

[ios_switches:vars]
ansible_network_os=cisco.ios.ios
ansible_connection=network_cli
ansible_user=admin
ansible_password=secret

[fmc_server]
fmc01 ansible_host=192.168.1.50

[fmc_server:vars]
ansible_network_os=cisco.fmcansible.fmc
ansible_connection=httpapi
ansible_httpapi_use_ssl=yes
ansible_httpapi_validate_certs=no
ansible_user=apiadmin
ansible_password=secret
playbook.yml (Example for IOS)
YAML
---
- name: Configure IOS Switch
  hosts: ios_switches
  gather_facts: no
  tasks:
    - name: Create a VLAN
      cisco.ios.ios_vlan:
        vlan_id: 10
        name: DATA_VLAN
        state: present

    - name: Save Configuration
      cisco.ios.ios_config:
        save_when: modified

